nd a raise will extract value from worse hands while discouraging draws. Opponent’s aggression suggests they may continue betting with draws or marginal hands, so raising builds the pot and takes control.\n\nAnswer: 400\n\nFinal Response:\n\nEvaluation: You hold two pair (Kings and Sevens), a strong hand on a relatively dry board. The opponent showed aggression by raising on the turn, indicating either a draw (like flush draw with hearts) or a strong hand (set, two pair). Raising to 400 increases pot commitment, penalizes draws, and extracts value from weaker pairs or draws. Folding is too weak, checking/calling invites danger on the river, and all-in is excessive. A moderate raise balances value and protection.\n\nReason: Raising to 400 maximizes expected value by building the pot when ahead and discouraging draws, while keeping worse hands in compared to an all-in.\n\nAnswer: 400'}
